---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Provincial Nominee Program Finder for Africans | AfriMigrate"
  description="Free guide to Canada's Provincial Nominee Programs (PNP). Compare all 11 provincial streams and find which one fits your profile as an African applicant."
>
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/canada">Canada</a> / PNP Finder</div>
  <div class="eyebrow">Canada · Provincial Nominee Program</div>
  <h1>Provincial Nominee Program Finder</h1>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    Every Canadian province except Quebec and Nunavut runs its own nominee stream, each with its own criteria. A nomination adds 600 points to your CRS score — enough to guarantee an Express Entry invitation. This is the route that works for most African applicants who don't score high enough in general draws.
  </p>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Popular With African Applicants</div>
    <h2>Where to look first</h2>
    <div class="tools-grid">
      <div class="tool-card">
        <div class="hot">Popular</div>
        <div class="tool-icon">🌾</div>
        <h3>Saskatchewan (SINP)</h3>
        <p>One of the most accessible PNPs, with an Occupation In-Demand list and an Express Entry sub-category that's well suited to skilled African workers.</p>
        <a href="/canada/pnp/saskatchewan-sinp" class="tool-link">See SINP points →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-card">
        <div class="tool-icon">🌲</div>
        <h3>Ontario (OINP)</h3>
        <p>Canada's largest province runs Human Capital Priorities, Skilled Trades, and Masters/PhD Graduate streams with regular targeted draws.</p>
        <span class="tool-link muted">Guide coming soon</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-card">
        <div class="tool-icon">🏔️</div>
        <h3>British Columbia (BC PNP)</h3>
        <p>Runs a weekly Skills Immigration draw system across tech, healthcare and general skilled worker categories.</p>
        <span class="tool-link muted">Guide coming soon</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-card">
        <div class="tool-icon">🌻</div>
        <h3>Manitoba (MPNP)</h3>
        <p>Uses an Expression of Interest system that favours applicants with a genuine connection or in-demand occupation.</p>
        <span class="tool-link muted">Guide coming soon</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">All Provinces</div>
    <h2>Every PNP at a glance</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Province</th><th>Streams</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Saskatchewan</td><td>SINP</td><td>Occupation In-Demand list, strong for African applicants</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Ontario</td><td>OINP</td><td>Human Capital, Skilled Trades, Masters/PhD Graduate</td></tr>
        <tr><td>British Columbia</td><td>BC PNP</td><td>Weekly Skills Immigration draws</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Manitoba</td><td>MPNP</td><td>Expression of Interest system</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Alberta</td><td>AAIP</td><td>Alberta Express Entry and Opportunity streams</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Nova Scotia</td><td>NSNP</td><td>Labour Market Priorities targeted draws</td></tr>
        <tr><td>New Brunswick</td><td>NBPNP</td><td>Express Entry and Skilled Worker streams</td></tr>
        <tr><td>PEI</td><td>PEI PNP</td><td>Small, competitive, frequent draws</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Newfoundland &amp; Labrador</td><td>NLPNP</td><td>Express Entry Skilled Worker stream</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Yukon</td><td>YNP</td><td>Employer-driven Skilled Worker stream</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Northwest Territories</td><td>NTNP</td><td>Employer-driven, small volume</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width: 700px; margin-top: 1rem;">
      Requirements and target occupation lists change frequently — always confirm current criteria on the province's official immigration website before applying.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
